Given $x_1,\ldots,x_n\in\ell_1$, either all the points coincide, or there exist a finite set $\mathcal B$, positive weights $(w_B)_{B\in\mathcal B}$, binary vectors $z_i\in\{0,1\}^{\mathcal B}$, and an affine map $T:\mathbb R^{\mathcal B}\to\ell_1$ with the following properties. For $$\|u\|_{1,w}=\sum_{B\in\mathcal B}w_B|u_B|,
 \qquad
 \|u\|_H^2=\sum_{B\in\mathcal B}w_Bu_B^2,$$ one has $$\begin{aligned}
 T(z_i)&=x_i,\label{eq:reconstruct}\\
 \|x_i-x_j\|_1
 &=\|z_i-z_j\|_{1,w}=\|z_i-z_j\|_H^2,
 \label{eq:cut-distance}\\
 \|T(u)-T(u')\|_1&\leq\|u-u'\|_{1,w}
 \qquad(u,u'\in\mathbb R^{\mathcal B}).\label{eq:contraction}
\end{aligned}$$ The space $H$ is $\mathbb R^{\mathcal B}$ with the indicated Hilbert norm.
